## When to use

- FAQ answers that readers scan by heading.
- Related settings sections with optional detail.
- Compact reference material with meaningful section titles.

## When not to use

- Use Collapsible for a single disclosure without grouped navigation.
- Use Tabs for peer views occupying one shared panel.
- Keep essential instructions visible rather than hiding them.

## API

### `Accordion`

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `value` / `defaultValue` | `Value[]` | uncontrolled / `[]` | Expanded item values. |
| `onValueChange` | `(value, details) => void` | — | Caller-owned controlled state. |
| `multiple` | `boolean` | `false` | Permit several expanded items. |
| `disabled` | `boolean` | `false` | Disable all items. |
| `orientation` | `"vertical" | "horizontal"` | `"vertical"` | Deprecated; retained as state only. |
| `keepMounted` | `boolean` | `false` | Keep closed panels in the DOM. |
| `hiddenUntilFound` | `boolean` | `false` | Allow browser find-in-page to reveal content. |

### `AccordionItem`

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `value` | `unknown` | generated | Stable identity for controlled state. |
| `disabled` | `boolean` | `false` | Disable this item's trigger. |

### `AccordionTrigger`

All Base UI Trigger props pass through, including `render`, `ref`, and `nativeButton`. A heading wraps
the trigger. Two decorative icons crossfade in place as `aria-expanded` changes; no rotation is animated.

### `AccordionContent`

All Base UI Panel props pass through, including `keepMounted`, `hiddenUntilFound`, `render`, `style`,
and `ref`. `className` styles the inner content, matching upstream; `style` applies to the panel.
Root and Item classes merge last.

## Motion contract

Authored intensity is **medium**: Each disclosure panel owns one measured block size, its retained content paint and an in-place glyph indicator; trigger and item paint stay local to their own region.

| Phase | Animated properties | Token | Interruptible |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Open / close / content resize | Measured block size clamped at zero; the primitive owns the open/close endpoint pair | `geometry.resize/measured` (`spring.morph`) | Yes, native reversal from the current size |
| Open / close; retained inner content paint | Opacity on the inner body only | `data.transition/one-shot` / `exit.fade/one-shot` | Yes, re-entry reverses the current paint |
| Expanded state | Two existing glyphs crossfade in place; no rotation, scale or path morph | `state.morph/one-shot` | Yes, the latest expanded state wins |
| Trigger focus/hover/disabled paint | Scoped foreground and border colour; focus and an unprovable palette are immediate | `state.color/css-transition` | Yes, latest committed colour |
| Item border paint | Scoped border colour on the item only | `state.color/css-transition` | Yes, latest committed colour |
| Plain trigger/content text | Changed graphemes only, no stagger | `text.change/changed-runs` | Yes, the newest diff replaces the old target |
| Direct numeric trigger/content quantity | Changed place values only | `number.roll/reels` | Yes, retargets the current reel |
| Later item insertion | One opacity envelope on that item | `data.transition/one-shot` | Yes, a presenting parent suppresses it |
| Initially open / reduced / none | Natural height and final paint, no entrance | `data.transition/one-shot` | Yes |

Base UI owns panel mounting, hidden state, the native disclosure endpoint pair, keyboard navigation, and
find-in-page behavior. The panel keeps one block-size owner: its native phase runs while the primitive opens or
closes, and the shared measured owner follows a direct plain-string content revision only while the panel is open
and idle. Reduced and none resolve the primitive's clock to zero, so a closing body commits immediately instead of
holding empty space. Rich caller children keep their native text identity.

## Accessibility

Triggers expose expanded state and control labelled regions. Focus stays on the trigger when a
panel toggles. Give each trigger a meaningful heading; do not place interactive controls inside it.
Disabled items are skipped in tab navigation. Content controls remain in normal tab order.

## Keyboard interactions

| Keys | Action |
| --- | --- |
| Enter / Space | Toggle the focused trigger. |
| Tab / Shift+Tab | Follow normal page order through triggers and open content. |

Base UI 1.6 follows the updated APG guidance without arrow-key roving focus. `orientation` and
`loopFocus` are deprecated passthrough props; neither changes keyboard focus behavior.

## Responsive behavior

The root fills its container. Long headings wrap and the icons retain their size. Content is
remeasured when wrapping changes; there is no fixed maximum height or breakpoint-specific state.

## Performance

T3 source ceiling: 12 KB gzip, an advisory reference under ADR-023 rather than a functional gate. One geometry
owner and one presence owner per mounted panel; closed panels unmount by default. Measurements run after commit
and on a direct plain-string content revision, never during render. No timers drive motion.
Server-rendered initially open content keeps its natural size before hydration.

## Notes for AI

- Use the Base UI array value API, not Radix `type="single"` or `collapsible` props.
- Preserve all four exports and the trigger-icon slot when customising.
- Keep the measurement wrapper and mode branch when editing motion.
- Related: Collapsible for a standalone disclosure; Tabs for alternate views.
